AmiWeather ABBS 3.3 Shell door
==============================

This is the runtime-qualified Shell-door integration for ABBS 3.3. It uses
the separate AmiWeatherDoor terminal frontend and the shared weather core.

Requirements
------------
Install AmiWeatherDoor, AmiSSL 5, a bsdsocket.library-compatible TCP/IP
stack, DNS, and Internet access. AmiWeatherDoor uses plain DOS stream I/O,
ASCII output, and its own bounded 32 KiB runtime stack. No manual Stack
command is required.

Installation
------------
Copy AmiWeatherDoor and AmiWeather.script into a fixed drawer such as
ABBS:Doors/AmiWeather/. Add the S line from Node0Config.example to the
appropriate NodeXConfig (or Node0Config fallback), and add matching menu text
from Node0Menu.example to Node0Menu/NodeXMenu. The number in the menu depends
on the entry's position among valid doors; it is not always 1.

The script passes no command-line context, runs the separate AmiWeatherDoor
executable, and always executes EndCLI afterward. Keep `failat 2147483647`
before the door invocation: ABBS warns that a broken Shell-door script can
expose an interactive shell if it stops before EndCLI.

The generic terminal UI supports H (hourly), D (daily), 7 (seven day), A
(fourteen day), W (details), L (location), R (refresh), and Q (return).
The no-argument launcher and interactive OPEN n session were qualified on the
ABBS 3.3 / AmigaOS 3.1 test system. Plain ASCII is the baseline; no ANSI
capability is required. FullName/NodeNr context passing is deliberately not
part of the qualified path.
